title: 'frame-support: Allow `cfg`-exclusive pallets to share an index'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `construct_runtime!` and `#[frame_support::runtime]` now accept two pallets with the same index
    when their `#[cfg]`s exclude each other, e.g. `#[cfg(debug_assertions)]` and
    `#[cfg(not(debug_assertions))]`. An index conflict is only reported when both pallets are part
    of the build, and the error points at both pallet names.

    Pallets can be gated on any `cfg` predicate. Before, only `feature` and `test` were taken into
    account for `AllPalletsWithSystem` and `AllPalletsWithoutSystem`, so pallets gated on anything
    else were left out of them. Malformed `#[cfg]`s are now reported by rustc at the attribute.
crates:
- name: frame-support-procedural
  bump: minor
- name: frame-support
  bump: minor
